text:
reena: Odd startup repro in the sample app: using jsonMode + schema coercion, after an auth retry the parsed object loses required fields. Raw body still correct.

alex: Which SDK and repro? Could be a coercion pass running before the final parse.

reena: sdk@0.25.0 in the sample. Repro (compact):
```js
const client = new RedwoodSDK({ jsonMode: true, coerce: true });
const res = await client.callFunction('user.settings', { uid: 'u7' }, {
  schema: { type: 'object', properties: { notifications: { type: 'object', properties: { email: { type: 'boolean' } }, required: ['email'] } }, required: ['notifications'] }
});
// If token expired: first 401 -> refresh -> 200
// Expect: res.parsed.notifications.email === true
// Observed: res.parsed === { notifications: {} }  // email dropped, but res.rawBody has the email: true
```
vince: Huh. So parse happens but coercion lost the field? Or parse short-circuited and a later coercion ran on a partially-initialized object. Do you see any log line about "skipping parse"?

reena: I grepped the logs 56 found a flag toggled in the retry handler: `sawAuthError = true` then parser checks `if (sawAuthError) return cachedParsed || {}`. That guard prevents full parse/coercion on the final success path.

tara: That matches another bug pattern we saw for streaming aborts; the guard was intended to avoid double-parse but accidentally persisted across retries. For coercion we need the final parse to run before any post-process. Workaround: set `coerce: false` or manually JSON.parse(res.rawBody) then run AJV coercion yourself. Not great for onboarding.

alex: Proposed fix: reset transient retry flags at the top of the HTTP client's retry-success branch before handing payload to the parse/coerce pipeline. Also add unit tests that combine auth-refresh + jsonMode + coerce=true + schema with nested required fields.

vince: Also add an integration test that simulates chunked JSON + auth refresh. If the parser/stream consumer was short-circuited we might lose chunks and coercion could run on an empty object.

reena: Filed issue: github.com/redwood-inference/sdk-js/issues/1477 - "jsonMode + coerce: required fields lost after auth retry" and linked a minimal repro and a suggested unit test. Tagging eng-runtime and devex.

bot-ci: Issue created (sdk-js #1477) by reena.

tara: I'll pick this up. Quick patch: clear `sawAuthError` immediately after a retry succeeds, and add the unit+integration tests. Also scan Py/Go SDKs for the same pattern.

reena: Thanks 64 I'll update the sample-app README with the temporary manual-parse workaround until the fix lands.
